The quadratic algorithms become completely impractical at $n = 50\,000$:
Bubble Sort takes over 155 seconds, while Quicksort does the same job
in 108 milliseconds --- roughly 1\,400 times faster. This matches the
theoretical prediction: the ratio of $n^2$ to $n \log n$ at
